WEBVTT

00:00:01.114 --> 00:00:04.134
That night Henry and George
ate fish and potatoes

00:00:04.134 --> 00:00:05.959
aboard Flying Scud.

00:00:05.959 --> 00:00:08.559
All five who left
the Grafton had survived.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.381
On the tenth of May the year before,

00:00:13.381 --> 00:00:17.056
the Invercauld had broken up
on the island’s northern coast.

00:00:17.056 --> 00:00:19.394
Nineteen of twenty-five reached land.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.318
Neither crew knew of the other.

00:00:25.318 --> 00:00:28.793
Andrew Smith wrote to his wife
about their sealskin boat.

00:00:28.793 --> 00:00:30.406
Two could take it out for food.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.382
In May of eighteen sixty-five,

00:00:36.382 --> 00:00:38.657
the Julian put in for repairs.

00:00:38.657 --> 00:00:40.832
Only George Dalgarno, Andrew Smith

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:43.022
and Robert Holding lived to go aboard.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.119
A few ribs of the Grafton still lie

00:00:49.119 --> 00:00:52.289
in the shingle at Carnley Harbour.

00:00:52.289 --> 00:00:54.314
Nearby, the stones of the hearth

00:00:54.314 --> 00:00:56.475
mark where the five made their home.

